{"version":"https://jsonfeed.org/version/1.1","title":"Hex - Tag | ꜱᴘᴀᴡɴ𝟐ᴘᴡɴ","description":"Personal CTF writeups and cybersecurity notes.","home_page_url":"https://ctf.spawn2pwn.my.id/","language":"en","icon":"https://ctf.spawn2pwn.my.id/apple-touch-icon.png","favicon":"https://ctf.spawn2pwn.my.id/favicon.ico","authors":[{"name":"spawn2pwn","url":"https://github.com/nfl-alvis","avatar":"https://ctf.spawn2pwn.my.id/images/IdaWin.png"}],"items":[{"title":"Sandi Berlapis","date_published":"2026-04-08T00:00:00&#43;07:00","date_modified":"2026-11-04T17:00:28&#43;07:00","id":"https://ctf.spawn2pwn.my.id/posts/sandi-berlapis/","url":"https://ctf.spawn2pwn.my.id/posts/sandi-berlapis/","authors":[{"name":"spawn2pwn","url":"https://github.com/nfl-alvis","avatar":"https://www.gravatar.com/avatar/b01c9af4b33ead25b072a03f8d0c5508?s=32&amp;d=mp"}],"tags":["Multi-stage Encoding","XOR","Base64","Hex","Reverse Engineering"],"summary":" A multi-layered cryptographic pipeline was used to obscure a confidential message. Can you reverse the transformations in the exact inverse order to recover the flag?\nTL;DR Sandi Berlapis is a cryptography challenge featuring a four-stage sequential encoding pipeline: XOR with a repeating key (PH4NT0M), byte reversal, Base64 encoding, and Hex encoding. Because all four transformations are deterministic and completely reversible, inverting the operations in reverse order (Hex Decode →\\rightarrow→ Base64 Decode →\\rightarrow→ Byte Reversal →\\rightarrow→ XOR) recovers the original flag. Encoder Mechanism Analysis The challenge provides the encryption script encoder.py:\n","content_html":"\u003cblockquote\u003e\n\u003cp\u003e\u003cstrong\u003eA multi-layered cryptographic pipeline was used to obscure a confidential message. Can you reverse the transformations in the exact inverse order to recover the flag?\u003c/strong\u003e\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003c/blockquote\u003e\n\u003cdiv class=\"details admonition abstract open\"\u003e\n    \u003cdiv class=\"details-summary admonition-title\"\u003e\u003ci class=\"icon fa-solid fa-clipboard-list\" aria-hidden=\"true\"\u003e\u003c/i\u003eTL;DR\u003ci class=\"details-icon fa-solid fa-angle-right\" aria-hidden=\"true\"\u003e\u003c/i\u003e\u003c/div\u003e\u003cdiv class=\"details-content\"\u003e\n      \u003cdiv class=\"admonition-content\"\u003e\u003cstrong\u003eSandi Berlapis\u003c/strong\u003e is a cryptography challenge featuring a four-stage sequential encoding pipeline: XOR with a repeating key (\u003ccode\u003ePH4NT0M\u003c/code\u003e), byte reversal, Base64 encoding, and Hex encoding. Because all four transformations are deterministic and completely reversible, inverting the operations in reverse order (\u003ccode\u003eHex Decode\u003c/code\u003e \u003cspan class=\"katex\"\u003e\u003cspan class=\"katex-mathml\"\u003e\u003cmath xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"\u003e\u003csemantics\u003e\u003cmrow\u003e\u003cmo\u003e→\u003c/mo\u003e\u003c/mrow\u003e\u003cannotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\"\u003e\\rightarrow\u003c/annotation\u003e\u003c/semantics\u003e\u003c/math\u003e\u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan class=\"katex-html\" aria-hidden=\"true\"\u003e\u003cspan class=\"katex-base\"\u003e\u003cspan class=\"katex-strut\" style=\"height:0.3669em;\"\u003e\u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan class=\"mrel\"\u003e→\u003c/span\u003e\u003c/span\u003e\u003c/span\u003e\u003c/span\u003e \u003ccode\u003eBase64 Decode\u003c/code\u003e \u003cspan class=\"katex\"\u003e\u003cspan class=\"katex-mathml\"\u003e\u003cmath xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"\u003e\u003csemantics\u003e\u003cmrow\u003e\u003cmo\u003e→\u003c/mo\u003e\u003c/mrow\u003e\u003cannotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\"\u003e\\rightarrow\u003c/annotation\u003e\u003c/semantics\u003e\u003c/math\u003e\u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan class=\"katex-html\" aria-hidden=\"true\"\u003e\u003cspan class=\"katex-base\"\u003e\u003cspan class=\"katex-strut\" style=\"height:0.3669em;\"\u003e\u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan class=\"mrel\"\u003e→\u003c/span\u003e\u003c/span\u003e\u003c/span\u003e\u003c/span\u003e \u003ccode\u003eByte Reversal\u003c/code\u003e \u003cspan class=\"katex\"\u003e\u003cspan class=\"katex-mathml\"\u003e\u003cmath xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"\u003e\u003csemantics\u003e\u003cmrow\u003e\u003cmo\u003e→\u003c/mo\u003e\u003c/mrow\u003e\u003cannotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\"\u003e\\rightarrow\u003c/annotation\u003e\u003c/semantics\u003e\u003c/math\u003e\u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan class=\"katex-html\" aria-hidden=\"true\"\u003e\u003cspan class=\"katex-base\"\u003e\u003cspan class=\"katex-strut\" style=\"height:0.3669em;\"\u003e\u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan class=\"mrel\"\u003e→\u003c/span\u003e\u003c/span\u003e\u003c/span\u003e\u003c/span\u003e \u003ccode\u003eXOR\u003c/code\u003e) recovers the original flag.\u003c/div\u003e\n    \u003c/div\u003e\n\u003c/div\u003e\n\u003ch2 class=\"heading-element\" id=\"encoder-mechanism-analysis\"\u003e\u003cspan\u003eEncoder Mechanism Analysis\u003c/span\u003e\n  \u003ca href=\"#encoder-mechanism-analysis\" class=\"heading-mark\"\u003e\n    \u003csvg class=\"octicon octicon-link\" viewBox=\"0 0 16 16\" version=\"1.1\" width=\"16\" height=\"16\" aria-hidden=\"true\"\u003e\u003cpath d=\"m7.775 3.275 1.25-1.25a3.5 3.5 0 1 1 4.95 4.95l-2.5 2.5a3.5 3.5 0 0 1-4.95 0 .751.751 0 0 1 .018-1.042.751.751 0 0 1 1.042-.018 1.998 1.998 0 0 0 2.83 0l2.5-2.5a2.002 2.002 0 0 0-2.83-2.83l-1.25 1.25a.751.751 0 0 1-1.042-.018.751.751 0 0 1-.018-1.042Zm-4.69 9.64a1.998 1.998 0 0 0 2.83 0l1.25-1.25a.751.751 0 0 1 1.042.018.751.751 0 0 1 .018 1.042l-1.25 1.25a3.5 3.5 0 1 1-4.95-4.95l2.5-2.5a3.5 3.5 0 0 1 4.95 0 .751.751 0 0 1-.018 1.042.751.751 0 0 1-1.042.018 1.998 1.998 0 0 0-2.83 0l-2.5 2.5a1.998 1.998 0 0 0 0 2.83Z\"\u003e\u003c/path\u003e\u003c/svg\u003e\n  \u003c/a\u003e\n\u003c/h2\u003e\u003cp\u003eThe challenge provides the encryption script \u003ccode\u003eencoder.py\u003c/code\u003e:\u003c/p\u003e"}]}